  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: Site Location Plan; 049_09_000A; 049_09_001; 049_09_010; 049_09_011A; 049_09_100A; 049_09_110A; 049_09_111D; 049_09_112A; 3 x Photographs of the Existing Shopfront; Covering Letter (Ref: DZ/KRI.9.1) from Monmouth Planning Ltd dated 24th November 2025 (x 5 pages); Design & Access Statement from Cake Architecture dated February 2026 (x 22 pages); Response Letter (Ref: DZ/KRI.1.9) from Monmouth Planning Ltd dated 10th February 2026 (x 6 pages); Image of the Gate Opened; Image of the Gate Closed; Image of Mineral Render Sample; Photograph of the Staircase dated 23rd January 2026.  \r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those of the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application. \r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policies D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017. \r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - The metalwork of the proposed shopfront shall be finished in a 'teapot brown' colour, as per images submitted as part of the submission.\r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policies D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017. "
  ],
